The attached image is relevant.
The attached image displays flow cytometry histograms showing the expression of costimulatory molecules CD40, CD80, and CD86 on dendritic cells. The black lines, representing cells treated with Nano-11, are shifted to the right compared to the gray lines (medium control), indicating increased expression of these markers. Specifically, Nano-11 markedly increased CD80 and CD86 expression and slightly increased CD40, demonstrating its ability to activate dendritic cells. This activation is a critical step in promoting an effective immune response by enabling DCs to present antigens and provide costimulatory signals to T cells, as elaborated in the PDF.